# DTF tier manifest: ci-oidc-exchange
#   (artifact-keeper#4031, #4511, #4314 shipped in 1.11.0; #4117 in 1.11.0;
#    #4663 and #4133 shipped in 1.11.1)
# Profile-set: filesystem + sso.mock-ci-oidc (a stdlib-python CI OIDC issuer
# serving discovery and JWKS over TLS at https://mock-ci-oidc/<iss>, trusted by
# the backend through CUSTOM_CA_CERT_PATH, and minting RS256 assertions with
# claims the oracle chooses on its http control port).
#
# POST /api/v1/auth/ci/token had never been called anywhere in this repo. The
# tier drives it end to end: AK fetches the mock's discovery and JWKS, verifies
# the signature, iss, aud, exp and nbf, matches the identity mapping's claim
# filters, provisions the mapping's service account and mints a session.
#
# THE BUGS
#   #4031  The account was named from the mapping but looked up by the token's
#          sub. GitLab/GitHub subs embed the ref, so the second ref of a
#          mapping hit 409 "Username already exists"; the same sub through two
#          issuers merged into one account; an exchange set is_active = true
#          again, undoing an administrator's deactivation; the account only
#          existed after a first exchange; deleting a mapping left it active.
#          Fixed (#4032): keyed on the mapping (external_id ci:<provider>:
#          <mapping>), created with the mapping, named in the create response
#          (service_account_id / service_account_username, ci-<12 hex>),
#          deactivation sticks (401), a mapping delete deactivates.
#   #4511  nbf was not checked: a not-yet-valid assertion exchanged. Fixed
#          (#4522) with the same 60 s skew leeway as exp.
#   #4314  A CI-exchanged credential could mint a permanent API token for its
#          service account on /profile/access-tokens and /auth/tokens. Fixed:
#          403 for any auth_provider = ci caller.
#   #4663  The verifier accepts an assertion up to 60 s past exp, and the
#          exchange capped the session at that passed exp: 200 with
#          expires_in: 0, a token session validation then accepted for its own
#          60 s leeway. Fixed (#4683): refused with 401 when less than 1 s of
#          validity remains, and AK's own tokens are validated with no leeway.
#   #4133  A provider could be given the Kubernetes API server's audience
#          (https://kubernetes.default.svc[.cluster.local]), accepting every
#          pod's default ServiceAccount token. Fixed (#4683): 400 naming it on
#          create and update, for every provider type, nothing written.
#   #4117  A mapping could not grant access (allowed_repo_ids is a ceiling).
#          Fixed (#4235): group_binding_ids makes the account a member of the
#          named groups on every mapping write and exchange, audited as
#          CI_OIDC_GROUP_BINDING_RECONCILED; [] strips; an unknown group is 400.
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) every image: a matching assertion exchanges (Bearer, ci- account,
#     expires_in 1..3600, /auth/me works; since #5054 a non-kubernetes token
#     is no longer capped at the assertion's exp, see ci-oidc-token-lifetime); a wrong
#     audience, wrong subject, wrong repository claim, a signature by a key the
#     JWKS does not publish, an assertion expired 300 s ago and a missing
#     header are 401, an unknown issuer is 404 naming it; an nbf 20 s ahead
#     (inside the skew) exchanges; the token reads the repository in the
#     mapping's allowed_repo_ids and is refused one the account is granted but
#     the ceiling excludes.
#   (FIX) #4031 x5, #4511, #4314, #4117 x2: RED on 1.10.0.
#         #4663 x2, #4133: RED on 1.10.0 and 1.11.0.
#   GREEN on 1.11.1 and later.
#
# NOT GATED: the #4133 startup `security` warning for a provider that already
# carries such an audience (it needs a provider written before an upgrade, or
# by SQL, and a backend restart), and the #4117 503 when a reconcile fails
# during an exchange (needs a DB fault mid-request).
#
# The #4663 own-token case exchanges through a kubernetes-type provider, the
# only type whose token still expires with its assertion after #5054.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~60 calls back to back. The oracle sleeps 13 s once
# (the #4663 own-token expiry).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem sso.mock-ci-oidc"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
